    <tags>backup disk-imaging imaging restore macrium recovery foss ntfs windows</tags>
    <summary>Free open-source disk imaging backup for Windows with Macrium image restore.</summary>
    <description>
OPBS (Open Pickle Backup System) is a free, open-source disk imaging backup
tool for Windows.

- Back up entire disks or partitions with differential chains, AES-256-GCM
  encryption and zstd compression
- Restores native `.opbs` images as well as Macrium Reflect 7/8 (`.mrimg`)
  and Reflect X (`.mrimgx`) images, including differential and incremental
  chains
- Read-only WinFsp mounts, file-level browse/extract, disk-to-disk clone
- Scheduled restore drills, bit-rot scrubbing with XOR parity
  self-healing, immutable repositories with off-box anchors
- Headless CLI for scripted environments

Installs per-user (no admin rights required, no machine-wide changes).
Silent install: `choco install opbs` (installer runs with `/S /currentuser`).
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/bobeire/opbs/releases/tag/0.6.87</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
